keywords:
  - "MCP security"
  - "tool poisoning"
  - "detector validation"
  - "replication"
  - "Model Context Protocol"
  - "measurement study"
abstract: >-
  Ecosystem-wide measurement of the public Model Context Protocol (MCP) registry:
  what fraction of public servers expose dangerous capabilities, and what fraction
  ship tool descriptions with patterns exploitable for tool poisoning. Heuristic
  detector outputs are candidates validated by manual review; reported precision is
  sample-scoped. Code, frozen data, and claim-verification scripts accompany this
  release.
